{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "heat_1d_nonuniform_neumann",
    "description": "MMS driver: 1-D heat equation u_t = alpha u_xx on the unit interval [0, 1] discretized on a SMOOTHLY STRETCHED non-uniform mesh by grids/cartesian_nonuniform_1d/rules/central_D2_nonuniform_neumann_bc (conservative finite-volume, inhomogeneous fixed-flux Neumann walls). Manufactured solution u(x,t) = x + exp(-alpha pi^2 t) cos(pi x): the linear ramp x has zero second derivative, and cos(pi x) gives u_xx = -pi^2 exp(-alpha pi^2 t) cos(pi x) with u_t = -alpha pi^2 exp(-alpha pi^2 t) cos(pi x), so u_t = alpha u_xx exactly with no forcing term. Its wall GRADIENT u_x = 1 - pi exp(-alpha pi^2 t) sin(pi x) equals the CONSTANT 1 at both walls (sin vanishes at x=0 and x=1), so the prescribed fluxes are qL = qR = 1, genuinely inhomogeneous (nonzero) Neumann. The discrete operator ANNIHILATES the linear ramp x exactly: every discrete face gradient of x is (x[j+1]-x[j])/(xc[j+1]-xc[j]) = 1, so the interior flux difference is 1-1=0 and, at the walls, the prescribed qL=qR=1 cancels the ramp's wall face gradient too; what remains is exactly the zero-flux evolution of the decaying cos mode (whose wall gradient is zero). Hence this Neumann problem's spatial error EQUALS the zero-flux problem heat_1d_nonuniform's error at every resolution while exercising the nonzero qL/qR terms. The mesh follows the grid's EDGE-ARRAY contract (grids/cartesian_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm): the consumer supplies ONE node array xe (shape [x_nodes], N+1 values) for the quadratic stretch x(xi) = 0.6 xi + 0.4 xi^2 on uniform computational nodes xi_k = (k-1)/N, i.e. xe[k] = 0.6 ((k-1)/N) + 0.4 ((k-1)/N)^2 (xe[1]=0, xe[N+1]=1), and the GRID derives the cell centers xc and control widths dxw from it via the nonuniform_cell_center / nonuniform_cell_width templates -- so xc and dxw cannot disagree, and a loader-API rebinding of N re-sizes x_nodes and re-derives the whole mesh consistently. The prescribed wall fluxes are the rule's free names qL, qR, declared here as ordinary real parameters with value 1 (matched to the manufactured ramp's unit wall gradient); the rule reads qL/qR only in its runtime body, never in the build-time ic/reference. The conservative FV Neumann Laplacian is second-order in the L2 norm on this smooth mesh (supraconvergence; verified L2 orders ~2.0), so the convergence gate checks L2 only, consistent with heat_1d_nonuniform. Initial condition and test references spell xc[i] = (xe(i-1)+xe(i))/2 inline from literals and N alone (the build-time 6.6.5/ic cellwise evaluation is scope-free; AGENTS.md build-time scope caveat; qL/qR are not referenced there), algebraically identical to the grid-derived xc observed used at runtime by the rule, so the t=0 assertion is exact.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_nonuniform_1d",
      "equation:heat",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Sections 2.12 (Neumann boundary conditions) and 2.13 (nonuniform grids) and the supraconvergence discussion."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Heat": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_nonuniform_1d/rules/central_D2_nonuniform_neumann_bc.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Temperature field over the x index set."
        },
        "alpha": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m^2/s",
          "default": 0.01,
          "description": "Thermal diffusivity."
        },
        "qL": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K/m",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Prescribed du/dx (+x direction) at the left wall x=xe[1] (the rule's Neumann free name). Set to 1 to match the manufactured ramp's unit wall gradient u_x(0)=1; nonzero, so the inhomogeneous left flux term is exercised."
        },
        "qR": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K/m",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Prescribed du/dx (+x direction) at the right wall x=xe[N+1] (the rule's Neumann free name). Set to 1 to match the manufactured ramp's unit wall gradient u_x(1)=1; nonzero, so the inhomogeneous right flux term is exercised."
        },
        "xe": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "x_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Node (edge) coordinates of the quadratic-stretch mesh, xe[k] = 0.6 ((k-1)/N) + 0.4 ((k-1)/N)^2 for node k = 1..N+1 (xe[1]=0, xe[N+1]=1): the grid's single geometry input, over the N+1-member node axis x_nodes. N is the document-scoped metaparameter substituted at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so a convergence-sweep rebinding of N re-derives the nodes. Aggregation index `k` (over x_nodes), distinct from the cell index.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "k"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "k": {
                "from": "x_nodes"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.6,
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "k",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "N"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.4,
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "k",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "N"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "k",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "N"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "xc": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Cell centers, GRID-DERIVED from xe by applying grids/cartesian_nonuniform_1d nonuniform_cell_center (xc[i] = (xe[i]+xe[i+1])/2). Read by the rule body for the center-to-center face-gradient denominators.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "nonuniform_cell_center",
            "bindings": {
              "xe": "xe"
            }
          }
        },
        "dxw": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Finite-volume control widths, GRID-DERIVED from xe by applying nonuniform_cell_width (dxw[i] = xe[i+1]-xe[i]). Read by the rule body as the outer control-cell divisor for both the interior flux difference and the Neumann wall faces. Because both xc and dxw descend from the same xe they are automatically consistent.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "nonuniform_cell_width",
            "bindings": {
              "xe": "xe"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": [
                  "i"
                ],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": {
                  "i": {
                    "from": "x"
                  }
                },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.5,
                    {
                      "op": "+",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] },
                            { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] },
                            { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "op": "cos",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      3.141592653589793,
                      {
                        "op": "aggregate",
                        "output_idx": [
                          "i"
                        ],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": {
                          "i": {
                            "from": "x"
                          }
                        },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            0.5,
                            {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "+",
                                  "args": [
                                    { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] },
                                    { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] }
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "+",
                                  "args": [
                                    { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] },
                                    { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "alpha",
              {
                "op": "D",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "D",
                    "args": [
                      "u"
                    ],
                    "wrt": "x"
                  }
                ],
                "wrt": "x"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_nonuniform_neumann_decay",
          "description": "Manufactured solution u(x,t) = x + exp(-alpha pi^2 t) cos(pi x) with alpha = 0.01 on the quadratic-stretch mesh (b=0.4), inhomogeneous Neumann qL=qR=1 (the unit wall gradient of the ramp x). The linear ramp is annihilated exactly by the discrete operator (every discrete face gradient of x equals 1, cancelled at the walls by qL=qR=1), so only the zero-flux evolution of the decaying cos mode carries error; cos(pi x) has zero wall gradient and u_t = alpha u_xx exactly, no forcing. References evaluate at the stretched cell centers xc[i] = (xe(i-1)+xe(i))/2, xe(k) = 0.6 (k/N)+0.4 (k/N)^2, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and the metaparameter N only; qL/qR are not referenced here), algebraically identical to the grid-derived xc observed. The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring; the t=0.1 assertion bounds the L2 error, which falls at the supraconvergent order 2 and equals the zero-flux problem heat_1d_nonuniform's error. Exact per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/heat_1d_nonuniform_neumann/golden/errors.json.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.1
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-09
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "aggregate",
                    "output_idx": [
                      "i"
                    ],
                    "args": [],
                    "ranges": {
                      "i": {
                        "from": "x"
                      }
                    },
                    "expr": {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        0.5,
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] },
                                { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] },
                                { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "cos",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          3.141592653589793,
                          {
                            "op": "aggregate",
                            "output_idx": [
                              "i"
                            ],
                            "args": [],
                            "ranges": {
                              "i": {
                                "from": "x"
                              }
                            },
                            "expr": {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                0.5,
                                {
                                  "op": "+",
                                  "args": [
                                    {
                                      "op": "+",
                                      "args": [
                                        { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] },
                                        { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] }
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "op": "+",
                                      "args": [
                                        { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] },
                                        { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] }
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.1,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 0.0001
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "aggregate",
                    "output_idx": [
                      "i"
                    ],
                    "args": [],
                    "ranges": {
                      "i": {
                        "from": "x"
                      }
                    },
                    "expr": {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        0.5,
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] },
                                { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] },
                                { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "exp",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "*",
                            "args": [
                              -0.01,
                              9.869604401089358,
                              0.1
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "cos",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "*",
                            "args": [
                              3.141592653589793,
                              {
                                "op": "aggregate",
                                "output_idx": [
                                  "i"
                                ],
                                "args": [],
                                "ranges": {
                                  "i": {
                                    "from": "x"
                                  }
                                },
                                "expr": {
                                  "op": "*",
                                  "args": [
                                    0.5,
                                    {
                                      "op": "+",
                                      "args": [
                                        {
                                          "op": "+",
                                          "args": [
                                            { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] },
                                            { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ { "op": "-", "args": [ "i", 1 ] }, "N" ] } ] }
                                          ]
                                        },
                                        {
                                          "op": "+",
                                          "args": [
                                            { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.6, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] },
                                            { "op": "*", "args": [ 0.4, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] }, { "op": "/", "args": [ "i", "N" ] } ] }
                                          ]
                                        }
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
